1
00:00:00,125 --> 00:00:05,877
FILING FOR LOVE

2
00:01:00,696 --> 00:01:01,864
What kind of dream was that?

3
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:13,459
<i>Did you get some rest?</i>

4
00:01:13,876 --> 00:01:16,587
<i>Don't forget to come in
at the usual time today. Good luck.</i>

5
00:01:16,879 --> 00:01:18,589
Oh, right. Work.

6
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,760
No wonder I had that terrible dream.

7
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,236
Here's your iced Americano.

8
00:01:42,113 --> 00:01:43,155
Mr. Noh.

9
00:01:43,531 --> 00:01:45,866
- Are you okay now?
- What do you mean?

10
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:48,160
When there was a ruckus outside
two days ago

11
00:01:48,536 --> 00:01:50,454
you passed out in shock.

12
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:54,417
The photos are everywhere.
They call you the Haemu Fainter.

13
00:01:55,459 --> 00:01:57,420
I heard the affair was real.

14
00:01:57,753 --> 00:01:59,630
So her husband is
Mr. Son from Food Brand Planning?

15
00:02:00,339 --> 00:02:02,300
What happens to them now?

16
00:02:02,508 --> 00:02:04,927
You handle the employees' affairs...

17
00:02:05,011 --> 00:02:06,304
- Da-yeong.
- Yes?

18
00:02:06,929 --> 00:02:08,639
I think your orders
are pretty backed up.

19
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:10,725
I'm so sorry.

20
00:02:15,688 --> 00:02:17,064
Hey, Mr. Noh.

21
00:02:17,857 --> 00:02:18,941
The Haemu Fainter.

22
00:02:20,693 --> 00:02:22,778
You look fine. Are you all right now?

23
00:02:22,862 --> 00:02:24,071
- I'm fine.
- Good.

24
00:02:24,155 --> 00:02:26,782
I heard you're in charge of affairs.
How did that happen?

25
00:02:26,866 --> 00:02:28,618
- I thought you were some big shot.
- Hey.

26
00:02:29,869 --> 00:02:31,454
I handle PM cases, not affairs.

27
00:02:31,662 --> 00:02:33,414
And the term is
"personal misconduct."

28
00:02:34,248 --> 00:02:35,416
You're just clueless.

29
00:02:43,341 --> 00:02:44,592
Mr. Noh.

30
00:02:49,513 --> 00:02:50,514
Yes, Ms. Park.

31
00:02:50,806 --> 00:02:53,225
I heard what happened.
Are you all right?

32
00:02:54,226 --> 00:02:55,269
I'm fine.

33
00:02:55,811 --> 00:02:56,937
That's good to hear.

34
00:03:04,654 --> 00:03:06,280
Hey, there, Mr. Noh.

35
00:03:06,781 --> 00:03:07,990
Are you just clocking in?

36
00:03:08,366 --> 00:03:10,409
I'm so pleased to see you,
I could faint.

37
00:03:13,788 --> 00:03:14,789
Ms. Joo.

38
00:03:15,665 --> 00:03:17,458
You can't tease me about that.

39
00:03:18,334 --> 00:03:20,127
Why not? Don't I have the right?

40
00:03:20,461 --> 00:03:23,089
The only reason you're fine
without a single scratch

41
00:03:23,297 --> 00:03:26,258
is that I caught you like this
with my two arms as you fell.

42
00:03:26,676 --> 00:03:28,761
You know I saved you, right?

43
00:03:30,388 --> 00:03:32,139
I sprained my wrist a bit,
so I got some acupuncture.

44
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:35,142
Sure, I can't thank you enough.

45
00:03:35,434 --> 00:03:36,560
It's nothing, really.

46
00:03:38,938 --> 00:03:41,732
I'll type up a report on what action
to take against Mr. Son.

47
00:03:42,483 --> 00:03:44,110
I took care of that already.

48
00:03:44,735 --> 00:03:45,778
What?

49
00:03:46,779 --> 00:03:48,114
I closed that case.

50
00:03:51,784 --> 00:03:53,953
Mouthwatering and mellow,
here's Masigo.

51
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:57,206
With Haemu's own
innovative food technology

52
00:03:57,289 --> 00:04:00,584
Masigo succeeded to realize
the farm-to-table notion

53
00:04:00,668 --> 00:04:02,211
and we're confident it will become

54
00:04:02,294 --> 00:04:05,131
a brand that represents Haemu
and leads global food trends.

55
00:04:05,423 --> 00:04:07,591
That concludes the presentation.
Thanks for listening.

56
00:04:12,096 --> 00:04:13,139
Thank you.

57
00:04:19,603 --> 00:04:20,646
Thank you.

58
00:04:20,938 --> 00:04:22,273
I'll do my best.

59
00:04:27,486 --> 00:04:29,697
<i>Even so, that's not right, Ms. Joo.</i>

60
00:04:30,698 --> 00:04:33,743
How could Ms. Jeong be demoted
to a plant while Mr. Son remains?

61
00:04:33,951 --> 00:04:35,619
And he gets to keep his project?

62
00:04:36,704 --> 00:04:39,498
If we must decide who did worse,
Ms. Jeong is single

63
00:04:39,582 --> 00:04:41,250
while Mr. Son's married,
so he did more harm.

64
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:43,169
Who did Mr. Son cause harm to?

65
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,255
Mr. Son always did well at work

66
00:04:46,338 --> 00:04:48,549
and he's in charge of a new brand
the Food Team has invested in.

67
00:04:48,924 --> 00:04:50,134
What about Ms. Jeong?

68
00:04:50,217 --> 00:04:51,969
All she did was play a part
in Mr. Son's project.

69
00:04:52,052 --> 00:04:53,512
Her performance and reputation
are below his.

70
00:04:54,388 --> 00:04:55,681
From the company's point of view

71
00:04:55,765 --> 00:04:58,100
Ms. Jeong has done more harm
than Mr. Son.

72
00:04:58,684 --> 00:04:59,727
Am I wrong?

73
00:05:01,312 --> 00:05:02,521
Still, morally speaking...

74
00:05:07,318 --> 00:05:08,360
Morals?

75
00:05:08,903 --> 00:05:10,780
Do you think
you're a police officer or a judge?

76
00:05:11,071 --> 00:05:13,866
Do companies reward the good
and punish the bad?

77
00:05:14,158 --> 00:05:16,285
A company only has to care

78
00:05:16,368 --> 00:05:18,829
about the profit or loss
caused by an employee.

79
00:05:18,913 --> 00:05:21,749
Because here,
that is our ethics and morals.

80
00:05:31,175 --> 00:05:32,259
What is it?

81
00:05:32,343 --> 00:05:34,345
Did you hope
for an exhilarating resolution?

82
00:05:34,845 --> 00:05:37,515
For a cheating couple
to be humiliated out of their jobs?

83
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,644
You're more naive than you look.

84
00:05:43,354 --> 00:05:44,647
Why did you put me in charge?

85
00:05:47,942 --> 00:05:48,984
This duty

86
00:05:50,319 --> 00:05:52,196
doesn't suit me because I'm naive.

87
00:05:58,369 --> 00:05:59,495
No, you're perfect for the job.

88
00:05:59,578 --> 00:06:01,956
- Ms. Joo, what on earth...
- Don't get too upset.

89
00:06:02,039 --> 00:06:04,083
Mr. Son got a bigger percentage
of his pay docked.

90
00:06:04,458 --> 00:06:07,336
Not to mention that this incident
ruined his reputation for good.

91
00:06:07,419 --> 00:06:09,922
It will be taken into consideration
at his next performance review.

92
00:06:10,422 --> 00:06:12,925
Plus, there are legal repercussions
if he's sued for divorce.

93
00:06:15,135 --> 00:06:17,513
There, let's forget
about a closed case.

94
00:06:17,596 --> 00:06:19,181
Do your next assignment right.

95
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:20,391
Sorry?

96
00:06:23,936 --> 00:06:24,937
"Work.com."

97
00:06:25,437 --> 00:06:27,189
You should check it out.
The comments are insane.

98
00:06:57,052 --> 00:07:01,724
EPISODE 2:
I AM THE BEST

99
00:07:02,308 --> 00:07:04,435
<i>Seriously, do something about Zone F.</i>

100
00:07:04,518 --> 00:07:06,186
<i>It's basically a love motel in Haemu.</i>

101
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,397
<i>- It's like watching porn.</i>
- "Zone F"?

102
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,565
<i>So everyone knows it.</i>

103
00:07:09,899 --> 00:07:11,483
{\an8}<i>The head office's
basement parking lot.</i>

104
00:07:12,067 --> 00:07:14,778
{\an8}<i>- It probably has no cameras.</i>
- What is this about?

105
00:07:14,862 --> 00:07:16,155
{\an8}<i>I never park there.</i>

106
00:07:16,238 --> 00:07:17,615
{\an8}Is this news to you?

107
00:07:18,866 --> 00:07:21,327
{\an8}It's Zone F in level four
of the basement parking lot.

108
00:07:21,994 --> 00:07:23,996
It's the spot
for couples in the company

109
00:07:24,079 --> 00:07:25,956
whether they're dating
morally or immorally.

110
00:07:26,498 --> 00:07:29,376
It's dark with no cameras
pointing that way

111
00:07:29,627 --> 00:07:31,170
and not many park that far down.

112
00:07:31,587 --> 00:07:32,671
It's perfect.

113
00:07:32,922 --> 00:07:35,007
You seem to know a lot, Mr. Cha.

114
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:37,635
That's what I heard
through the grapevine.

115
00:07:38,510 --> 00:07:39,970
Let's check the facts first.

116
00:07:40,429 --> 00:07:42,348
We can't investigate
based on a rumor.

117
00:07:42,431 --> 00:07:43,557
- Yes, sir.
- Okay?

118
00:07:43,641 --> 00:07:45,267
Check facts? With whom?

119
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:47,686
Our team has set up

120
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:50,230
- a humint network.
- What? "Humint"?

121
00:07:50,314 --> 00:07:51,357
INFO GATHERED FROM INFORMANTS

122
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:54,151
- Yes.
<i>- Gosh, don't even talk about it.</i>

123
00:07:54,234 --> 00:07:55,444
<i>There's no end to it.</i>

124
00:07:55,527 --> 00:07:58,405
<i>It's embarrassing for both parties
if we catch them in the act.</i>

125
00:07:58,948 --> 00:08:00,449
<i>We just turn a blind eye.</i>

126
00:08:00,532 --> 00:08:03,619
<i>I heard Zone F is the place to go.</i>

127
00:08:03,702 --> 00:08:06,830
BASEMENT PARKING CLOSED
FOR REPAIR WORK

128
00:08:06,914 --> 00:08:07,957
It's that spot over there.

129
00:08:08,832 --> 00:08:10,960
Is it more thrilling
if they do it there?

130
00:08:11,502 --> 00:08:13,963
I don't know why people
with decent jobs would do that.

131
00:08:16,006 --> 00:08:17,299
I wonder myself.

132
00:08:17,383 --> 00:08:19,551
If you see anything suspicious

133
00:08:19,635 --> 00:08:20,928
please report it to us.

134
00:08:21,011 --> 00:08:23,847
- Sure thing. Take care, then.
- Thank you.

135
00:08:26,684 --> 00:08:30,270
Our humint network confirmed
the rumor is true.

136
00:08:34,024 --> 00:08:35,609
Humint, my foot.

137
00:08:37,611 --> 00:08:39,488
- Let's go eat.
- Okay.

138
00:08:39,571 --> 00:08:42,199
The cafeteria's serving pork cutlet,
<i>doenjang </i>soup

139
00:08:42,282 --> 00:08:43,367
- braised potatoes...
- Not there.

140
00:08:43,450 --> 00:08:45,577
I'll check my list
of nearby restaurants.

141
00:08:45,953 --> 00:08:47,204
Don't bother.

142
00:08:52,126 --> 00:08:54,670
THIS EVENING

143
00:08:59,383 --> 00:09:01,051
What are you doing today?
It's your birthday.

144
00:09:01,719 --> 00:09:02,845
Did your boyfriend schedule a date?

145
00:09:03,679 --> 00:09:04,680
Well...

146
00:09:04,763 --> 00:09:06,890
Why are you so mysterious?

147
00:09:07,141 --> 00:09:09,977
I'm curious what kind of guy
girls like you date.

148
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:50,476
Why does the cafeteria food
get worse by the day?

149
00:09:50,642 --> 00:09:53,062
- Right? Let's eat out tomorrow.
- Okay.

150
00:09:53,353 --> 00:09:54,813
- Ms. Yeon.
- What?

151
00:09:54,897 --> 00:09:57,316
Isn't that Mr. Kwon, your husband?

152
00:09:57,983 --> 00:09:59,193
Yes, that's right.

153
00:09:59,276 --> 00:10:00,986
Why don't you even say hi?

154
00:10:01,779 --> 00:10:02,905
Did you two fight?

155
00:10:04,281 --> 00:10:06,033
We didn't fight. We get along fine.

156
00:10:06,366 --> 00:10:08,452
Ji-yeon, wait until you get married.

157
00:10:08,535 --> 00:10:09,578
After just a few years

158
00:10:09,828 --> 00:10:11,455
you flinch
when your hands accidentally touch.

159
00:10:11,955 --> 00:10:12,998
That's an exaggeration.

160
00:10:16,668 --> 00:10:17,961
You two are hilarious.

161
00:10:18,295 --> 00:10:20,506
Before you got married,
you didn't say hi

162
00:10:20,589 --> 00:10:21,924
because you were dating in secret.

163
00:10:22,007 --> 00:10:23,675
But now,
everyone knows you're married.

164
00:10:24,218 --> 00:10:25,511
Are you shy now that you're married?

165
00:10:25,594 --> 00:10:27,137
We're keeping work
and personal lives separate.

166
00:10:27,888 --> 00:10:31,183
You speak as if
your private life is pretty eventful.

167
00:10:34,019 --> 00:10:35,020
Hey.

168
00:10:35,979 --> 00:10:37,022
Do you guys even do it?

169
00:10:37,523 --> 00:10:38,524
Stop it.

170
00:10:39,441 --> 00:10:40,901
You don't do that with family.

171
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,238
You used to be so fired up.

172
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:46,740
Why does it die
once people get married?

173
00:10:47,199 --> 00:10:49,243
You burn to death
if you stay fired up.

174
00:10:58,043 --> 00:10:59,711
NEW MESSAGE FROM YEON
FROM GENERAL AFFAIRS

175
00:11:01,046 --> 00:11:03,173
<i>I'm meeting old friends from school
and will be home late.</i>

176
00:11:04,633 --> 00:11:05,717
<i>Okay.</i>

177
00:11:20,732 --> 00:11:22,568
Oh, dear. I'm so sorry, Mr. Kwon.

178
00:11:23,235 --> 00:11:25,946
- It's okay.
- I'm so stupid.

179
00:11:26,029 --> 00:11:27,781
I'm really sorry.

180
00:11:27,865 --> 00:11:29,616
Don't be. It happens.

181
00:11:30,951 --> 00:11:31,952
Ms. Seon?

182
00:11:32,494 --> 00:11:33,662
I'm coming, sir.

183
00:11:34,204 --> 00:11:35,372
- Sorry.
- Go ahead.

184
00:11:58,228 --> 00:12:00,022
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

185
00:12:04,985 --> 00:12:06,528
I'm loving this.

186
00:12:07,029 --> 00:12:08,155
- Right?
- Jun-seo!

187
00:12:08,822 --> 00:12:11,116
- Over here.
- He looks even better now.

188
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,243
- Long time no see.
- You haven't changed at all.

189
00:12:13,452 --> 00:12:16,163
Sorry, I forgot to tell you
he was coming.

190
00:12:17,706 --> 00:12:18,749
Don't worry.

191
00:12:18,999 --> 00:12:20,709
It's been ages since we broke up.

192
00:12:29,092 --> 00:12:30,552
It has been a while, So-young.

193
00:12:30,886 --> 00:12:31,929
Yes.

194
00:12:32,137 --> 00:12:33,972
You look just the same.

195
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,682
You haven't changed.

196
00:12:36,975 --> 00:12:39,269
I'm not the same. I got old, right?

197
00:12:39,353 --> 00:12:40,437
No.

198
00:12:40,771 --> 00:12:42,522
You're pretty. Just like before.

199
00:12:43,649 --> 00:12:46,068
- What's going on here?
- You're prettier now.

200
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:49,071
- You're just the same.
- I lost my appetite.

201
00:12:49,905 --> 00:12:51,490
- Sorry.
- Pour me a drink?

202
00:12:51,990 --> 00:12:53,033
Here.

203
00:12:54,701 --> 00:12:55,827
<i>Let's begin.</i>

204
00:13:01,917 --> 00:13:03,377
<i>You can vote now.</i>

205
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,962
FINAL RESULT
OF THE THIRD SURVIVOR

206
00:13:05,963 --> 00:13:07,172
Why did his ranking drop?

207
00:13:07,256 --> 00:13:10,175
<i>Vote for the person
who stole your heart.</i>

208
00:13:12,094 --> 00:13:13,929
The mission benefit is too great.

209
00:13:14,012 --> 00:13:17,557
<i>BOYS II PLANET's first round
of the final global vote is now open.</i>

210
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:20,102
<i>BOYS II PLANET's final global...</i>

211
00:13:20,185 --> 00:13:21,895
Can I vote for the same person twice?

212
00:13:21,979 --> 00:13:23,689
<i>Log onto the BOYS II PLANET site</i>

213
00:13:24,648 --> 00:13:25,816
<i>and click "vote"</i>

214
00:13:26,358 --> 00:13:28,485
<i>- then select one participant.</i>
- Who's that?

215
00:13:33,615 --> 00:13:35,909
Hi. Let's have a drink.
It's been a while.

216
00:13:48,422 --> 00:13:50,757
What are you up to?
Do you want to get back with me?

217
00:13:52,259 --> 00:13:53,343
Do you want to?

218
00:13:54,428 --> 00:13:55,554
Forget it, then.

219
00:13:56,722 --> 00:13:59,641
Gosh.
You're really one-sidedly one-sided.

220
00:14:00,267 --> 00:14:02,602
You asked me out
then suddenly ghosted me.

221
00:14:03,228 --> 00:14:05,105
Now you barge in after two years

222
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:07,107
- and want a drink?
- So what?

223
00:14:07,691 --> 00:14:09,234
Were you sad that I dumped you?

224
00:14:10,068 --> 00:14:11,278
Did you cry over me?

225
00:14:12,154 --> 00:14:13,447
You didn't.

226
00:14:13,530 --> 00:14:15,991
"If you want to leave, go ahead.
I won't hold you back."

227
00:14:16,575 --> 00:14:18,869
I bet you didn't even shed a tear.

228
00:14:19,703 --> 00:14:21,204
Here. have a drink and call it even.

229
00:14:32,966 --> 00:14:33,967
It's good, isn't it?

230
00:14:36,261 --> 00:14:37,429
It's not bad.

231
00:14:39,222 --> 00:14:40,891
Let me stay for a while.

232
00:14:42,392 --> 00:14:44,186
- What?
- Let me stay here.

233
00:14:44,978 --> 00:14:46,271
The whiskey's the rent.

234
00:14:46,688 --> 00:14:48,023
This costs over three million won.

235
00:14:48,106 --> 00:14:50,275
Hey, what kind of nonsense is this?

236
00:14:50,776 --> 00:14:52,819
Get out. This isn't a boarding house.

237
00:14:52,903 --> 00:14:54,738
I really don't have a place to go.

238
00:14:54,988 --> 00:14:58,450
I had to leave my old place
and I couldn't find a new place yet.

239
00:14:58,742 --> 00:15:00,202
You know that my family...

240
00:15:01,203 --> 00:15:02,871
They're no help to me at all.

241
00:15:04,581 --> 00:15:06,124
I get that you're in a tough spot...

242
00:15:06,375 --> 00:15:09,002
You can't barge
into a guy's bachelor pad.

243
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:13,673
- I'll get you a hotel room.
- For how long?

244
00:15:14,091 --> 00:15:15,634
Who knows how long I'll need?

245
00:15:16,176 --> 00:15:17,302
Do you have ten million won?

246
00:15:22,808 --> 00:15:24,559
I guess you can't help me.

247
00:15:25,227 --> 00:15:26,853
I get it. I'll leave.

248
00:15:27,729 --> 00:15:31,358
I'll stay at a sauna
or end up on some street corner.

249
00:15:31,441 --> 00:15:34,152
And if a creepy guy hits on me?

250
00:15:34,236 --> 00:15:36,154
I'll go with him. I can't be picky.

251
00:15:37,489 --> 00:15:38,532
Goodbye.

252
00:15:49,501 --> 00:15:50,585
It's only for the time being.

253
00:15:51,253 --> 00:15:52,671
Leave as soon as you can.

254
00:15:56,591 --> 00:15:59,052
I'll take the small room.
You can take the big room.

255
00:16:03,598 --> 00:16:06,101
Wait, isn't that a given?

256
00:16:09,312 --> 00:16:10,939
How brazen.

257
00:16:17,946 --> 00:16:20,031
Take a look at the shower head.
It's leaking again.

258
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:22,576
Okay, I will.

259
00:16:24,744 --> 00:16:26,246
You say that and do nothing.

260
00:16:27,622 --> 00:16:28,665
Goodness.

261
00:16:29,458 --> 00:16:32,752
Did you read about Zone F online?

262
00:16:34,504 --> 00:16:35,964
Yes, I did.

263
00:16:37,924 --> 00:16:39,509
Some people have too much energy.

264
00:16:40,093 --> 00:16:42,846
They do something at work
that we don't even do in bed.

265
00:17:00,697 --> 00:17:01,740
Shall we do it?

266
00:17:06,828 --> 00:17:08,330
I'm tired.

267
00:17:13,043 --> 00:17:14,628
I wasn't interested, either.

268
00:17:16,046 --> 00:17:17,088
Turn off the light.

269
00:17:17,422 --> 00:17:18,673
You do it.

270
00:17:35,649 --> 00:17:37,984
You've lost weight.
Your face got smaller.

271
00:17:39,152 --> 00:17:41,154
Are you stressed out
because of Joo In-a?

272
00:17:43,156 --> 00:17:44,824
Drink the whiskey you brought.

273
00:17:44,908 --> 00:17:46,076
Don't touch my beer.

274
00:17:47,494 --> 00:17:49,037
Do you hate her that much?

275
00:17:50,455 --> 00:17:51,498
Why?

276
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:53,250
Because she made you handle affairs?

277
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:55,126
They're PM cases, not affairs.

278
00:17:56,044 --> 00:17:58,630
Ms. Joo doesn't know about me yet.

279
00:17:58,713 --> 00:18:00,590
I was working on something
on Team One.

280
00:18:01,299 --> 00:18:04,052
I put everything in the folder
and when she sees that

281
00:18:05,345 --> 00:18:07,347
she'll see how good I am
and reappoint me.

282
00:18:07,430 --> 00:18:08,598
If she's that competent.

283
00:18:10,642 --> 00:18:11,726
Think about it.

284
00:18:12,018 --> 00:18:14,729
She wouldn't want to waste
talent like mine on stupid cases.

285
00:18:14,813 --> 00:18:17,190
Why not? I think
you're perfect for the job.

286
00:18:17,732 --> 00:18:19,317
To handle the PM cheaters.

287
00:18:19,401 --> 00:18:20,777
Why me?

288
00:18:23,238 --> 00:18:24,698
- Hang on.
<i>- You are</i>

289
00:18:25,031 --> 00:18:26,408
the best one for the job.

290
00:18:29,536 --> 00:18:30,579
Hey.

291
00:18:31,871 --> 00:18:34,165
That's exactly what Joo In-a said,
that I was the best for the job.

292
00:18:35,166 --> 00:18:37,711
- Why am I best for the job?
- It's about couples in love.

293
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:41,423
- That's your expertise.
- What does she know about me?

294
00:18:42,257 --> 00:18:44,301
We just met. She can't know...

295
00:18:46,511 --> 00:18:47,554
No way.

296
00:18:48,305 --> 00:18:49,389
That retreating figure...

297
00:18:53,893 --> 00:18:55,020
Did she see me?

298
00:18:57,856 --> 00:18:59,733
So the reason she chose me...

299
00:19:01,735 --> 00:19:02,777
was that?

300
00:19:05,739 --> 00:19:07,490
<i>No, it can't be.</i>

301
00:19:09,534 --> 00:19:10,577
<i>Can it be?</i>

302
00:19:12,412 --> 00:19:13,413
<i>Is it?</i>

303
00:19:15,123 --> 00:19:16,291
<i>Long, straight hair.</i>

304
00:19:17,584 --> 00:19:18,710
<i>A white shirt.</i>

305
00:19:26,593 --> 00:19:27,844
It's practically a uniform.

306
00:19:47,030 --> 00:19:48,114
<i>I can't say for sure.</i>

307
00:19:49,324 --> 00:19:50,492
<i>I don't think it was her.</i>

308
00:19:58,333 --> 00:19:59,668
Why were you staring at me?

309
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,212
Is a ghost haunting me?

310
00:20:02,295 --> 00:20:03,672
I came to make myself some coffee.

311
00:20:06,299 --> 00:20:08,635
You look like
you have something to say.

312
00:20:08,968 --> 00:20:10,095
Mr. Noh.

313
00:20:10,178 --> 00:20:12,597
If you have any concerns,
you can come to me freely.

314
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:16,351
<i>Yes, rather than driving myself crazy</i>

315
00:20:16,434 --> 00:20:17,602
<i>I'll ask her and clear the air.</i>

316
00:20:18,144 --> 00:20:19,854
- Ms. Joo.
<i>- Wait.</i>

317
00:20:22,399 --> 00:20:24,609
<i>I can't ask if she saw me kiss.</i>

318
00:20:26,528 --> 00:20:27,529
What is it?

319
00:20:29,197 --> 00:20:30,824
What should we do
about the basement parking lot?

320
00:20:30,907 --> 00:20:34,494
We've confirmed through our humint
that it's a real issue.

321
00:20:34,869 --> 00:20:37,414
Shall we put up a sign saying
personal misconduct isn't allowed?

322
00:20:37,497 --> 00:20:38,707
We can't say we did any work, then.

323
00:20:39,249 --> 00:20:41,459
- We have to expose them.
- Expose?

324
00:20:41,668 --> 00:20:43,461
How am I going to do that?

325
00:20:43,545 --> 00:20:45,255
I can't go on a stakeout
just to wait for it.

326
00:20:45,338 --> 00:20:46,339
A stakeout?

327
00:20:46,673 --> 00:20:47,924
A stakeout?

328
00:20:48,258 --> 00:20:50,719
Why would you say something
so nonsensical?

329
00:20:50,802 --> 00:20:54,013
We're not detectives.
Why would we go on a stakeout?

330
00:20:54,806 --> 00:20:56,891
- Right, exactly.
- Exactly.

331
00:20:57,225 --> 00:20:59,227
I heard that someone
on the Audit Team

332
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:01,646
flew a drone and took photos.

333
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:05,900
How could an auditor do that?
We're not some drone-flying club.

334
00:21:11,698 --> 00:21:13,116
Down your coffee and get moving.

335
00:21:14,425 --> 00:21:15,801
My poor legs.

336
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:21,682
This was the only company car
left for us to take.

337
00:21:22,767 --> 00:21:25,394
Darn it. I should've brought my car.

338
00:21:25,853 --> 00:21:28,356
Still, if you push the seat
back a bit

339
00:21:28,439 --> 00:21:29,649
it should free up some space.

340
00:21:29,732 --> 00:21:31,484
- No, it's fine.
- Let me help you.

341
00:21:31,776 --> 00:21:33,319
It's fine, really. I...

342
00:21:36,906 --> 00:21:38,532
I'm so sorry, Mr. Noh.

343
00:21:55,216 --> 00:21:57,093
Jeez, what the heck
are we even doing?

344
00:21:58,094 --> 00:21:59,762
Okay, Hyun-kyu.

345
00:22:00,137 --> 00:22:03,307
You didn't do all that studying
for your degree

346
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:05,935
just to do this kind of job, did you?

347
00:22:07,561 --> 00:22:11,065
Unlike you,
I didn't go to a good university

348
00:22:11,148 --> 00:22:12,900
nor have great credentials.

349
00:22:14,026 --> 00:22:15,778
I barely got this job
because I'm from the area

350
00:22:15,861 --> 00:22:17,321
where Haemu built a huge factory.

351
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:19,448
Oh, during my interview I said

352
00:22:20,199 --> 00:22:21,742
"White blood runs through my veins."

353
00:22:23,035 --> 00:22:25,413
That's how I introduced myself,
and they liked how I was different.

354
00:22:27,915 --> 00:22:30,042
- "White blood."
- White blood.

355
00:22:31,544 --> 00:22:33,254
- By white, you meant Haemu's color?
- Yes.

356
00:22:33,879 --> 00:22:35,673
That's why they call you
"White Blood Cell."

357
00:22:35,756 --> 00:22:36,757
That's right.

358
00:22:40,302 --> 00:22:44,056
You know, competent people like you

359
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:47,101
might feel bored
by what our team does.

360
00:22:47,184 --> 00:22:50,354
But working at Haemu
which everyone envies

361
00:22:50,438 --> 00:22:55,026
and being on the Audit Team,
the best team in the company

362
00:22:55,317 --> 00:22:57,445
makes me pleased and proud.

363
00:23:11,709 --> 00:23:12,918
Hey, White Blood Cell.

364
00:23:13,335 --> 00:23:14,378
Yes, Mr. Noh?

365
00:23:15,129 --> 00:23:17,631
I didn't doze off.
I was only blinking for a long time.

366
00:23:17,715 --> 00:23:18,758
Do you remember

367
00:23:19,425 --> 00:23:20,926
the day Ms. Joo first joined?

368
00:23:25,598 --> 00:23:27,933
Do you know what she was wearing?

369
00:23:28,893 --> 00:23:30,186
Just a moment.

370
00:23:30,728 --> 00:23:33,522
- I remember such details perfectly.
- Do you?

371
00:23:34,774 --> 00:23:36,150
See if you can remember.

372
00:23:37,735 --> 00:23:38,736
What was she wearing?

373
00:23:40,071 --> 00:23:41,197
She wore

374
00:23:43,157 --> 00:23:44,325
black pants.

375
00:23:46,702 --> 00:23:48,746
What about her top?

376
00:23:49,205 --> 00:23:50,247
Her top...

377
00:23:51,791 --> 00:23:52,833
It was black.

378
00:23:54,293 --> 00:23:55,586
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

379
00:23:58,214 --> 00:23:59,256
It was black.

380
00:24:02,468 --> 00:24:03,511
Or not.

381
00:24:04,929 --> 00:24:06,514
I think it was a white shirt.

382
00:24:07,765 --> 00:24:08,766
Hey.

383
00:24:10,184 --> 00:24:11,185
Are you saying she wore white?

384
00:24:13,312 --> 00:24:14,396
Maybe not.

385
00:24:14,939 --> 00:24:16,774
- What?
- Was it black?

386
00:24:17,691 --> 00:24:19,735
- Was it black?
- No.

387
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:21,862
It was white.

388
00:24:22,446 --> 00:24:23,489
Yes, white.

389
00:24:24,573 --> 00:24:25,699
Why, you!

390
00:24:28,119 --> 00:24:29,161
It was definitely white.

391
00:24:30,579 --> 00:24:31,664
Am I mistaken?

392
00:24:32,832 --> 00:24:34,166
Forget I even asked.

393
00:24:34,959 --> 00:24:38,045
- I'll go get coffee, so sober up.
- Okay.

394
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,450
I have a bad feeling about this.

395
00:25:11,829 --> 00:25:13,581
Gosh, what am I even doing?

396
00:25:14,623 --> 00:25:16,959
So what if she saw it? I don't care.

397
00:25:17,418 --> 00:25:20,462
It's not like I committed a crime.
Forget it.

398
00:25:21,422 --> 00:25:22,464
Oh, my gosh.

399
00:25:24,925 --> 00:25:26,177
Why are you so startled?

400
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:31,056
You walked in so suddenly.

401
00:25:33,017 --> 00:25:34,852
Can't I walk in suddenly?

402
00:25:35,436 --> 00:25:37,104
Should I have knocked?

403
00:25:39,982 --> 00:25:41,066
What?

404
00:25:41,650 --> 00:25:42,651
Were you

405
00:25:44,778 --> 00:25:45,946
doing this again?

406
00:26:04,548 --> 00:26:05,633
What was that?

407
00:26:07,801 --> 00:26:10,346
So she saw it. She saw everything.

408
00:26:49,677 --> 00:26:50,719
Noh Ki-jun.

409
00:26:52,471 --> 00:26:53,555
What do you want?

410
00:26:54,098 --> 00:26:55,599
You told me to ignore you at work.

411
00:26:55,683 --> 00:26:57,142
It's just us now.

412
00:26:57,810 --> 00:26:59,436
Is it Joo In-a again?

413
00:26:59,728 --> 00:27:00,854
You look half-dead.

414
00:27:00,938 --> 00:27:01,939
Yes.

415
00:27:02,481 --> 00:27:04,275
Bury me on a sunny slope.

416
00:27:05,234 --> 00:27:06,694
Why are you thinking
of getting buried?

417
00:27:07,319 --> 00:27:08,612
You have a lifeline.

418
00:27:09,154 --> 00:27:10,239
Director Kim.

419
00:27:11,115 --> 00:27:13,284
His dinner with the VP got canceled

420
00:27:13,367 --> 00:27:14,994
and he seemed to be looking
for a drinking buddy.

421
00:27:31,552 --> 00:27:32,845
Hello, Director Kim.

422
00:27:33,595 --> 00:27:35,764
It's Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun.

423
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:48,193
Ms. Joo talks back
to every senior executive.

424
00:27:48,444 --> 00:27:51,030
Does she think I'm staying still
because I can't speak up?

425
00:27:51,447 --> 00:27:54,325
- I'm just keeping my boundaries.
- Yes, you're right.

426
00:27:55,326 --> 00:27:56,910
Is she rude to the executives, too?

427
00:27:57,745 --> 00:28:00,914
I guess she's not the type
to bow to the powerful.

428
00:28:00,998 --> 00:28:05,586
I don't care how she treats
the powerful or powerless.

429
00:28:06,754 --> 00:28:07,838
And there's you.

430
00:28:07,921 --> 00:28:10,299
She has such
a poor judgment of character.

431
00:28:10,758 --> 00:28:13,761
You're our ace, Mr. Noh.

432
00:28:13,844 --> 00:28:15,804
Yet she dumped you in Team Three.

433
00:28:16,221 --> 00:28:19,183
Now, you're handling PM cases.
What the heck is PM, anyway?

434
00:28:19,266 --> 00:28:20,267
Exactly.

435
00:28:20,934 --> 00:28:22,895
I'm having the worst time, sir.

436
00:28:23,228 --> 00:28:25,981
Don't you worry about that.

437
00:28:26,899 --> 00:28:27,900
You know who I am.

438
00:28:28,901 --> 00:28:31,195
Let me tell you something

439
00:28:31,653 --> 00:28:33,572
that's still off the record.

440
00:28:39,661 --> 00:28:42,790
I'm working to create
a new department.

441
00:28:44,208 --> 00:28:50,839
It'll serve as the control tower
of the whole organization.

442
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:54,134
Business General... No.

443
00:28:54,218 --> 00:28:57,262
It's called
the General Business Control HQ.

444
00:28:57,346 --> 00:28:59,973
General Business Control HQ.

445
00:29:01,308 --> 00:29:03,143
- What a great name.
- Right?

446
00:29:04,812 --> 00:29:06,939
I said I wanted you on the team.

447
00:29:07,773 --> 00:29:10,567
You'll be able to escape soon.

448
00:29:15,030 --> 00:29:17,282
- Let me pour you a drink, sir.
- Okay.

449
00:29:20,202 --> 00:29:21,829
A toast

450
00:29:22,496 --> 00:29:25,416
to our General Business

451
00:29:25,499 --> 00:29:27,626
- Control HQ.
- Control HQ.

452
00:29:27,793 --> 00:29:31,130
- Let's drink to its bright future.
- Cheers!

453
00:29:40,347 --> 00:29:41,557
I'm in the mood.

454
00:29:55,779 --> 00:29:56,864
I'm heading home.

455
00:29:56,947 --> 00:29:58,532
Bye. See you tomorrow.

456
00:30:02,453 --> 00:30:04,705
IT DEVELOPMENT TEAM
ASSISTANT MANAGER KWON HYUN-WOO

457
00:30:04,788 --> 00:30:06,123
<i>It's raining.</i>

458
00:30:06,206 --> 00:30:07,249
<i>When do you get off work?</i>

459
00:30:10,836 --> 00:30:11,879
<i>I'm working late.</i>

460
00:30:12,254 --> 00:30:13,547
<i>Buy an umbrella and head home.</i>

461
00:30:32,691 --> 00:30:33,859
Hello?

462
00:30:37,738 --> 00:30:38,739
Jun-seo?

463
00:30:41,033 --> 00:30:42,493
We did that all the time.

464
00:30:43,452 --> 00:30:44,578
Back then...

465
00:30:45,871 --> 00:30:47,164
we were young and rash.

466
00:30:47,748 --> 00:30:48,916
I'm glad I called you.

467
00:30:57,174 --> 00:30:59,134
Are you sure
you don't need to eat dinner?

468
00:30:59,593 --> 00:31:01,345
You love to eat.

469
00:31:02,054 --> 00:31:03,805
I'm okay with anything
if I'm with you.

470
00:31:08,143 --> 00:31:09,186
Right.

471
00:31:14,274 --> 00:31:15,651
It's pouring.

472
00:31:24,785 --> 00:31:26,453
- Why don't we...
- Yes?

473
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:28,163
stay together?

474
00:31:29,373 --> 00:31:30,624
Just until the rain stops.

475
00:32:00,946 --> 00:32:02,281
SEND
IT DEVELOPMENT TEAM, KWON HYUN-WOO

476
00:32:05,284 --> 00:32:06,451
Sent.

477
00:32:08,161 --> 00:32:09,496
Great work.

478
00:32:09,830 --> 00:32:11,248
My gosh. You must be tired.

479
00:32:11,498 --> 00:32:12,624
Great work until late.

480
00:32:12,708 --> 00:32:15,085
Don't mention it. I'm feeling proud.

481
00:32:15,502 --> 00:32:17,170
Today was
the first overtime of my life.

482
00:32:18,088 --> 00:32:19,089
Really?

483
00:32:19,715 --> 00:32:20,757
In that case

484
00:32:21,258 --> 00:32:22,509
why don't we grab a drink
to celebrate?

485
00:32:22,593 --> 00:32:23,885
I'd love to.

486
00:32:24,177 --> 00:32:25,470
Let's eat
something delicious, Mr. Kwon.

487
00:32:25,554 --> 00:32:27,472
- Okay, let's wrap up and leave.
- Great!

488
00:32:36,356 --> 00:32:37,691
WIFE

489
00:32:48,368 --> 00:32:49,745
I said you could leave first.

490
00:32:53,332 --> 00:32:54,374
Were you rained on?

491
00:33:01,340 --> 00:33:02,591
We shouldn't do this.

492
00:33:07,846 --> 00:33:09,264
The rain has stopped.

493
00:33:11,558 --> 00:33:12,559
Let's do it.

494
00:33:13,101 --> 00:33:14,686
- What?
- Let's do it.

495
00:33:16,146 --> 00:33:17,648
We can't keep going like this.
We have to do it.

496
00:33:18,273 --> 00:33:19,483
What's with you?

497
00:33:22,194 --> 00:33:24,488
All right. Let's go home first.
You're going to catch a cold.

498
00:33:25,656 --> 00:33:26,698
Let's do it here.

499
00:33:27,157 --> 00:33:28,950
It's that area. Zone F.

500
00:33:39,544 --> 00:33:40,545
Hey.

501
00:33:47,094 --> 00:33:48,720
- What's with you?
- Be quiet.

502
00:34:29,302 --> 00:34:30,637
DIRECTOR KIM HAN-SU

503
00:34:30,721 --> 00:34:32,264
<i>The president approved!</i>

504
00:34:32,347 --> 00:34:35,016
<i>You'll be out of the Audit Team
within days, Mr. Noh.</i>

505
00:34:35,100 --> 00:34:37,561
Director Kim, you're awesome!

506
00:34:41,231 --> 00:34:43,442
<i>I'm the best</i>

507
00:34:44,943 --> 00:34:46,695
<i>I'm the best</i>

508
00:34:47,988 --> 00:34:50,073
- Are you getting off early today?
- I'll try to.

509
00:34:50,407 --> 00:34:51,616
- Let's eat something good.
- Okay.

510
00:34:51,992 --> 00:34:53,910
- Try to clock out quickly.
- Okay.

511
00:34:58,749 --> 00:35:01,126
- Hello. Good morning.
- Hello.

512
00:35:06,256 --> 00:35:08,508
- The weather's great, isn't it?
- Yes.

513
00:35:09,426 --> 00:35:12,053
You're looking extra sharp today.

514
00:35:12,763 --> 00:35:13,972
- Do I?
- Yes.

515
00:35:14,723 --> 00:35:16,683
You two look great, too.

516
00:35:18,018 --> 00:35:19,436
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

517
00:35:31,907 --> 00:35:32,908
Hello, Ms. Joo.

518
00:35:33,492 --> 00:35:34,951
Hey, Mr. Noh. Good morning.

519
00:35:35,410 --> 00:35:37,746
You must like dress shirts.
You look good in them.

520
00:35:39,831 --> 00:35:41,041
You're looking happy.

521
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,043
Did something great happen
this morning?

522
00:35:43,293 --> 00:35:45,212
There's no reason
to be in a foul mood.

523
00:35:45,295 --> 00:35:46,630
Look at that great weather.

524
00:35:46,713 --> 00:35:48,089
There is a reason, actually.

525
00:35:49,174 --> 00:35:51,301
You haven't caught
a single case in the parking garage.

526
00:35:52,427 --> 00:35:54,763
You won't take matters lightly
just like you did

527
00:35:54,846 --> 00:35:56,473
with Mr. Son's case, will you?

528
00:35:57,641 --> 00:35:58,683
Keep it up, will you?

529
00:35:58,767 --> 00:36:01,561
Every assignment is important
here in the Audit Team.

530
00:36:02,646 --> 00:36:05,857
<i>Fine, I'll go along. I won't have
to see her for much longer.</i>

531
00:36:06,149 --> 00:36:07,442
Yes, of course.

532
00:36:07,734 --> 00:36:10,070
I even brought my car
to stake out properly.

533
00:36:10,529 --> 00:36:12,155
Will I ever let you down again?

534
00:36:13,281 --> 00:36:14,449
No, never.

535
00:36:22,791 --> 00:36:23,875
Ms. Joo.

536
00:36:24,251 --> 00:36:27,337
There was a huge lucky draw
at our online mall recently

537
00:36:27,546 --> 00:36:30,131
and people are asking
how the winners were decided

538
00:36:30,215 --> 00:36:32,342
or if the draw was even real,
and some are complaining

539
00:36:32,425 --> 00:36:34,177
that they didn't win
even after many tries.

540
00:36:34,261 --> 00:36:36,972
It's not like the Audit Team
is the customer service center.

541
00:36:37,055 --> 00:36:39,808
Mr. Noh, you can continue
to work on the parking lot case.

542
00:36:40,141 --> 00:36:41,393
Wait a second.

543
00:36:41,852 --> 00:36:44,104
You'll need a partner
for your stakeout, won't you?

544
00:36:44,813 --> 00:36:46,690
Goodness. One second.

545
00:36:47,607 --> 00:36:50,235
White Blood Cell is on the phone too.
We don't have enough manpower.

546
00:36:51,820 --> 00:36:53,405
We do, Mr. Moo.

547
00:36:54,072 --> 00:36:55,740
We have our strongest asset here.

548
00:36:57,617 --> 00:36:58,618
Who?

549
00:37:06,877 --> 00:37:08,670
You're making me feel uncomfortable.
Cut it out.

550
00:37:11,089 --> 00:37:14,217
Why? Is the parking lot case
not quite suitable for you?

551
00:37:16,469 --> 00:37:19,764
But you told me that every case here
is equally important.

552
00:37:25,186 --> 00:37:26,354
Shall I do that, then?

553
00:37:27,105 --> 00:37:29,649
Let's spend some quality time alone.

554
00:37:37,908 --> 00:37:39,492
You don't need to buckle up.

555
00:37:40,368 --> 00:37:41,411
I'm not starting the car.

556
00:37:44,247 --> 00:37:45,373
It's my decision.

557
00:37:45,457 --> 00:37:47,167
Come on. You forgot, didn't you?

558
00:37:47,667 --> 00:37:49,377
Unbuckle it.
It must be uncomfortable.

559
00:37:49,461 --> 00:37:51,338
No, I'm not uncomfortable at all.

560
00:37:51,421 --> 00:37:53,465
I feel so comfortable right now.

561
00:37:53,548 --> 00:37:55,717
Unbuckle it. You don't need
to play it cool over this matter.

562
00:37:57,928 --> 00:37:59,262
Things happen.

563
00:37:59,638 --> 00:38:02,557
Stakeouts are for people
who are experienced.

564
00:38:02,766 --> 00:38:03,975
It's all right.

565
00:38:06,311 --> 00:38:09,898
I knew it. Your understanding
of these assignments is very high.

566
00:38:09,981 --> 00:38:10,982
Sorry?

567
00:38:12,233 --> 00:38:14,110
I'm sure you know a thing or two

568
00:38:14,194 --> 00:38:16,529
about cases like this one.

569
00:38:19,908 --> 00:38:20,951
Ms. Joo.

570
00:38:21,660 --> 00:38:24,788
- Back then, that...
- That? What do you mean by that?

571
00:38:24,871 --> 00:38:27,082
That. Whatever it is you saw.

572
00:38:27,457 --> 00:38:28,500
It wasn't that...

573
00:38:29,084 --> 00:38:31,378
I'm not that kind of person.

574
00:38:31,628 --> 00:38:33,421
My lips were also...

575
00:38:34,506 --> 00:38:35,548
Quiet.

576
00:38:37,008 --> 00:38:38,051
Over there.

577
00:39:02,242 --> 00:39:03,243
Okay.

578
00:39:18,174 --> 00:39:20,468
I'll wrap it up. It's my job.

579
00:39:32,897 --> 00:39:35,150
I'll open the door.
I'm from the Audit Team.

580
00:39:44,117 --> 00:39:45,660
I'm opening the door.

581
00:39:53,418 --> 00:39:55,754
Oh, my. Director Kim!

582
00:39:56,254 --> 00:39:57,380
You said you were busy.

583
00:40:00,050 --> 00:40:02,427
- Wait.
- What are you two doing here?

584
00:40:02,510 --> 00:40:03,511
What's with you?

585
00:40:04,846 --> 00:40:07,307
You, of all people,
should know better.

586
00:40:07,390 --> 00:40:10,310
When you both have spouses,
don't you?

587
00:40:13,438 --> 00:40:15,732
Will you close that door?

588
00:40:16,775 --> 00:40:18,276
Wrap it up and come outside.

589
00:40:27,035 --> 00:40:28,495
I knew it, Mr. Noh.

590
00:40:28,745 --> 00:40:30,663
I knew you could do it!

591
00:40:31,247 --> 00:40:34,459
You caught a big one.
He's a big fish!

592
00:40:34,959 --> 00:40:37,128
This is why you're the ace
of the Audit Team.

593
00:40:38,296 --> 00:40:39,339
Let's see.

594
00:40:39,672 --> 00:40:43,051
Director Kim was
formerly your direct superior.

595
00:40:45,386 --> 00:40:48,223
You took down your former superior
whom you worked with for years

596
00:40:48,890 --> 00:40:50,725
like a cold-blooded man!

597
00:40:51,392 --> 00:40:53,019
If only everyone else were like you

598
00:40:53,103 --> 00:40:56,856
this world would've been
a much better place.

599
00:41:04,322 --> 00:41:05,573
Excuse me, Ms. Joo.

600
00:41:06,116 --> 00:41:08,868
Is there a possibility
that Director Kim will be let off

601
00:41:08,952 --> 00:41:11,287
- just like Mr. Son?
- No.

602
00:41:11,704 --> 00:41:13,581
This is a different case.

603
00:41:14,165 --> 00:41:16,709
He's an executive, so we can revoke
his contract and fire him right away.

604
00:41:16,793 --> 00:41:18,128
Fire him?

605
00:41:19,129 --> 00:41:21,714
But Director Kim is also
a necessary part of the company...

606
00:41:21,798 --> 00:41:23,216
Not at all.

607
00:41:23,550 --> 00:41:25,677
He's an old-timer with an ego
who sits around doing nothing

608
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:27,137
only because
he's close to the president.

609
00:41:27,971 --> 00:41:29,722
He must've been an eyesore
to the vice president.

610
00:41:30,974 --> 00:41:34,561
You just gave him
a wonderful reason to fire that man.

611
00:41:39,899 --> 00:41:41,025
Director Kim

612
00:41:43,403 --> 00:41:44,404
is done for.

613
00:42:13,141 --> 00:42:15,518
DIRECTOR KIM HAN-SU

614
00:42:18,229 --> 00:42:21,024
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to...</i>

615
00:42:33,161 --> 00:42:35,955
ELDEST SISTER
ACCEPT

616
00:42:36,039 --> 00:42:37,707
- <i>Hilarious.</i>
- Hey.

617
00:42:38,249 --> 00:42:41,085
<i>Hello, Ki-jun? When are you coming?</i>

618
00:42:41,878 --> 00:42:43,838
I'm on my way, and I'm almost there.

619
00:42:48,384 --> 00:42:51,262
Ki-jun, we have to change
the bathroom doorknob, too.

620
00:42:51,554 --> 00:42:52,597
Okay.

621
00:42:54,224 --> 00:42:55,266
Hey, Ki-jun!

622
00:42:55,683 --> 00:42:57,477
Take a look at Jin-yeong's laptop.

623
00:42:58,061 --> 00:42:59,771
- Laptop?
- Hey, Ki-jun.

624
00:42:59,854 --> 00:43:01,356
That couch has been wobbling.
Take a look.

625
00:43:01,731 --> 00:43:04,567
I'm only one man,
so talk to me one at a time.

626
00:43:06,277 --> 00:43:07,278
The couch?

627
00:43:09,322 --> 00:43:11,115
- Which side is wobbly?
- The left.

628
00:43:11,199 --> 00:43:12,450
Goodness.

629
00:43:14,577 --> 00:43:18,206
Goodness, I'm so proud of you,
my youngest one.

630
00:43:20,875 --> 00:43:22,835
Cut it out, Mom.

631
00:43:29,092 --> 00:43:30,635
Mom, this meat is delicious.

632
00:43:34,264 --> 00:43:36,182
Hey, Ki-jun.
Why are you drinking so much?

633
00:43:36,266 --> 00:43:38,017
Look at him.
He hasn't even eaten his food.

634
00:43:38,101 --> 00:43:39,352
You can't even hold your alcohol.

635
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:43,398
- Stop drinking.
- Stop pinching me, please!

636
00:43:44,107 --> 00:43:45,400
Will you just leave me alone?

637
00:43:45,483 --> 00:43:46,985
Is something going on, Ki-jun?

638
00:43:47,235 --> 00:43:48,528
Right? What's wrong?

639
00:43:49,195 --> 00:43:50,822
Hey, is someone bullying you?

640
00:43:51,864 --> 00:43:54,742
What? Hey, who is it?
Who's that punk?

641
00:43:54,826 --> 00:43:56,703
Hey, go file a lawsuit.

642
00:43:56,786 --> 00:43:58,454
- Talk to her husband!
- I'll talk to him.

643
00:43:58,538 --> 00:44:00,498
We have to talk it out first.
Do you want me to make a call?

644
00:44:00,581 --> 00:44:03,001
Please stop this and leave me alone.

645
00:44:03,084 --> 00:44:05,003
We need the name first. Who is it?

646
00:44:05,086 --> 00:44:07,130
- We have to talk it out first.
- Talk what out?

647
00:44:07,213 --> 00:44:09,007
Look at this kid.

648
00:44:09,090 --> 00:44:11,301
Call your husband first, okay?

649
00:44:11,384 --> 00:44:14,429
Who's the punk that did this
to my precious son?

650
00:44:15,138 --> 00:44:16,431
- You...
- Darn it.

651
00:44:16,514 --> 00:44:17,849
- Who is it?
- Talk it out.

652
00:44:17,932 --> 00:44:19,934
- Hey, tell me who it is.
- We need the name first.

653
00:44:20,018 --> 00:44:21,894
- What's the name?
- Mom, listen.

654
00:44:21,978 --> 00:44:24,063
- We need the name first.
- We need that.

655
00:44:24,147 --> 00:44:25,398
- Who is it?
- Why won't he pick up?

656
00:44:25,481 --> 00:44:26,774
- Get the name.
- We need the name.

657
00:44:26,858 --> 00:44:28,234
You all need to stop.

658
00:44:28,318 --> 00:44:30,111
- Who is it? Tell me!
- Hear me out.

659
00:44:30,194 --> 00:44:32,989
- Ki-jun.
- I hate all three of you!

660
00:44:33,072 --> 00:44:35,325
Just leave me alone!

661
00:44:35,408 --> 00:44:37,827
No, bring her phone to me.

662
00:44:38,036 --> 00:44:40,246
- Is he not picking up?
- Call the customer service line.

663
00:44:40,330 --> 00:44:42,832
- The customer service?
- We need to reach someone!

664
00:44:57,972 --> 00:45:00,183
HAEMU PHARMACEUTICAL
2025 CONTRACT INSPECTION

665
00:45:00,266 --> 00:45:01,976
2024 FUND EXECUTION INSPECTION

666
00:45:05,355 --> 00:45:07,023
NOH KI-JUN, AUDIT TEAM 1 TURNOVER

667
00:45:07,106 --> 00:45:11,819
DO YOU WISH TO PERMANENTLY DELETE
ALL FOLDERS AND FILES?

668
00:45:31,589 --> 00:45:34,133
I'm sorry about Director Kim.

669
00:45:34,217 --> 00:45:36,302
- Did you dig him up intentionally?
- No.

670
00:45:37,261 --> 00:45:38,721
It was a coincidence
from another case.

671
00:45:38,805 --> 00:45:39,806
How disappointing.

672
00:45:40,098 --> 00:45:41,808
I thought you finally learned
to wield your sword

673
00:45:41,891 --> 00:45:43,017
but it was sheer luck.

674
00:45:44,310 --> 00:45:46,187
I haven't given you anything yet.

675
00:45:46,854 --> 00:45:47,897
Prove yourself

676
00:45:48,606 --> 00:45:49,899
that you're different from your mom.

677
00:46:13,631 --> 00:46:15,925
Honey, Sung-yeol is here.

678
00:46:17,301 --> 00:46:19,512
You should say hi to him.
I'll go and make coffee.

679
00:46:22,306 --> 00:46:24,142
Father, your youngest son is here.

680
00:46:25,810 --> 00:46:28,479
- And so are you, Jae-yeol.
- It's been a while.

681
00:46:30,940 --> 00:46:32,275
How's your health, Father?

682
00:46:32,817 --> 00:46:34,986
I've exiled you
and haven't called you back.

683
00:46:35,403 --> 00:46:37,029
How dare you show yourself here?

684
00:46:37,113 --> 00:46:38,739
It's great to see
that you're the same.

685
00:46:41,451 --> 00:46:43,536
How come there is
no middle ground between you two?

686
00:46:43,953 --> 00:46:46,289
One of you is too soft
to do anything substantial

687
00:46:46,622 --> 00:46:50,126
and the other is too reckless,
causing trouble everywhere.

688
00:46:50,543 --> 00:46:51,544
Darn it.

689
00:46:53,129 --> 00:46:55,256
You see, Father

690
00:46:56,257 --> 00:46:57,758
I have caused yet another trouble.

691
00:46:59,469 --> 00:47:01,971
It's the gas plant in Saudi Arabia
that you've even dreamed of.

692
00:47:02,054 --> 00:47:05,057
I got the first package,
and on top of that the third one.

693
00:47:05,391 --> 00:47:08,102
The entire project
is worth 8.77 billion dollars.

694
00:47:09,020 --> 00:47:10,146
And I got it.

695
00:47:17,361 --> 00:47:20,281
So? Isn't this good enough
to put an end to my exile?

696
00:47:21,616 --> 00:47:23,576
I hear there's a spot open
in the head office.

697
00:47:39,967 --> 00:47:41,302
Should I cancel the luncheon?

698
00:47:41,677 --> 00:47:43,137
You do not look well.

699
00:47:44,388 --> 00:47:45,431
I'm fine.

700
00:47:48,017 --> 00:47:49,977
I need personnel evaluation reports

701
00:47:50,478 --> 00:47:52,188
and a list of potential staff
up for a promotion.

702
00:47:52,980 --> 00:47:54,023
Also, set up

703
00:47:54,565 --> 00:47:57,485
a dinner with QS International's
President Lee Hyeong-geun

704
00:47:57,860 --> 00:47:58,861
as soon as possible.

705
00:47:59,403 --> 00:48:00,613
I understand.

706
00:48:01,906 --> 00:48:04,408
Would you like to leave right away
for the AI camp?

707
00:48:05,493 --> 00:48:06,494
In half an hour.

708
00:48:08,829 --> 00:48:09,914
One second.

709
00:48:32,019 --> 00:48:33,479
I can do this for myself.

710
00:48:35,106 --> 00:48:36,274
E-mail me the files.

711
00:48:39,860 --> 00:48:40,861
Yes, sir.

712
00:49:18,774 --> 00:49:21,152
- What now?
- I'm telling you.

713
00:49:24,363 --> 00:49:25,906
Goodness, I need some sugar.

714
00:49:28,868 --> 00:49:29,869
My gosh.

715
00:49:31,787 --> 00:49:34,749
Where was Ms. Yoon's snack box again?

716
00:49:36,250 --> 00:49:38,252
There it is. Ms. Yoon's snack box.

717
00:49:39,420 --> 00:49:42,590
Goodness. It's heavy.
Did you get something new?

718
00:49:43,966 --> 00:49:45,551
Hey, these are new.

719
00:49:49,680 --> 00:49:50,681
It's good.

720
00:49:52,016 --> 00:49:53,059
- Mango-flavored?
- Yes.

721
00:49:53,392 --> 00:49:55,811
Hey, Hae-young. Where are we
having team dinner again?

722
00:49:55,895 --> 00:49:57,355
Piggy's Charcoal BBQ.

723
00:49:57,438 --> 00:49:58,439
We're having pork again?

724
00:49:58,939 --> 00:50:01,609
Can we get something better?
It's Ms. Joo's welcome party.

725
00:50:01,692 --> 00:50:03,986
Our budget for team dinners
is running low this year.

726
00:50:04,278 --> 00:50:05,738
Ms. Pyun.

727
00:50:06,155 --> 00:50:08,324
Why do you act like
a stingy mother-in-law

728
00:50:08,407 --> 00:50:11,160
who never lets anyone near her money
with the company fund?

729
00:50:12,286 --> 00:50:14,455
There's a servant
that's trying to clean out the fund

730
00:50:14,789 --> 00:50:16,123
so I have no other choice, Mr. Moo.

731
00:50:16,207 --> 00:50:17,208
- What?
- Servant?

732
00:50:17,541 --> 00:50:18,584
You heard her, right?

733
00:50:18,668 --> 00:50:20,127
Did you just call me a servant?

734
00:50:20,211 --> 00:50:22,880
- Do you feel guilty?
- Technically, we're all servants.

735
00:50:23,881 --> 00:50:24,965
Anyway.

736
00:50:25,549 --> 00:50:27,176
Where's Mr. Noh?
He's been away for a while.

737
00:50:27,259 --> 00:50:29,720
Mr. Noh didn't seem well.

738
00:50:29,804 --> 00:50:32,598
He doesn't look well,
he keeps sighing

739
00:50:32,973 --> 00:50:35,643
and his eyes looked a bit watery too.

740
00:50:36,227 --> 00:50:38,646
- Anyway, he looks quite sad.
- Really?

741
00:50:39,730 --> 00:50:41,899
- Did he get dumped?
- I think so.

742
00:50:41,982 --> 00:50:44,110
Goodness. That's heartbreaking.

743
00:50:48,656 --> 00:50:50,032
Thanks a lot.

744
00:51:10,302 --> 00:51:11,345
<i>He is</i>

745
00:51:11,971 --> 00:51:13,055
<i>leaving.</i>

746
00:51:18,728 --> 00:51:19,854
<i>My hope.</i>

747
00:51:21,230 --> 00:51:22,440
<i>My lifeline.</i>

748
00:51:25,443 --> 00:51:26,569
Adios.

749
00:51:27,630 --> 00:51:29,617
PIGGY'S CHARCOAL BBQ

750
00:51:29,641 --> 00:51:30,642
Hello.

751
00:51:30,849 --> 00:51:32,016
Thank you.

752
00:51:38,326 --> 00:51:40,745
It used to be a great spot.

753
00:51:41,746 --> 00:51:43,748
Back then, the front of the factory
used to be salt farms.

754
00:51:43,831 --> 00:51:45,500
It became a huge issue.

755
00:51:45,583 --> 00:51:47,835
What's the most important
when it comes to making salt?

756
00:51:47,919 --> 00:51:49,003
Sunlight and wind.

757
00:51:49,671 --> 00:51:51,631
So if the southeastern direction
gets blocked off

758
00:51:52,173 --> 00:51:54,509
it creates a shadow
and stops the wind

759
00:51:54,592 --> 00:51:55,885
which stops salt from crystallizing.

760
00:51:56,552 --> 00:51:59,639
And the one who stepped up
as a troubleshooter was...

761
00:51:59,722 --> 00:52:00,807
Mr. Baek.

762
00:52:01,432 --> 00:52:04,394
- You should eat some, too.
- I've been eating. It's okay.

763
00:52:04,602 --> 00:52:07,855
You're making me look rude.

764
00:52:07,939 --> 00:52:09,148
After all, I'm the youngest.

765
00:52:10,817 --> 00:52:12,485
No, it's all right, really.

766
00:52:12,944 --> 00:52:15,530
Because everyone thinks
you're just like that.

767
00:52:15,613 --> 00:52:16,906
That I'm just rude?

768
